  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the User Goal**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core request: designing a web app that allows interactive exploration of DUSP S.R.L.\'s diesel injection spare parts. The crucial element will be the hand gesture control via webcam, which I\'ll integrate with product image display. I\'m focusing on user interaction as the main goal.\n\n\n**Developing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now sketching the system architecture, aiming for a simulated 3D environment using WebGL/Three.js. My plan includes pulling product details from `db.json` and enriching them with real-time internet searches. It\'s designed for big screen projection, so I\'m prioritising low latency and high performance, with WebAssembly in mind. I need to map the provided images (1063.jpg, etc.) to the database entries. The constraints boil down to a single-view application design.\n\n\n**Refining the UI/UX**\n\nI\'m solidifying the single-view concept: a carousel with 3D-ish models and a detail overlay fulfills the interactive presentation needs perfectly. My tech stack will be Tailwind CSS, React with Vite. A backend is now essential for dynamic internet searches (Gemini with search grounding via a custom tool), required by the user\'s prompt.\n\n\n**Implementing the API**\n\nI\'m now building the backend API endpoint with Express to serve the Vite app and enrich product data. I\'ve chosen MediaPipe for vision and hand gesture recognition, planning to use the NPM package `@mediapipe/tasks-vision` within the React frontend. For the 3D presentation, I\'m leaning heavily on `three.js`, `@react-three/fiber`, and `@react-three/drei`, to create a visually appealing 3D carousel effect using textured planes from the available 2D images.\n\n\n**Defining API Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the backend, designing an API endpoint that queries Gemini with Google Search to summarize product info based on the name or category. I\'m focusing on the JSON parsing from `db.json` and image mapping to ensure I store and link them effectively, and I have saved the images into `public/images/`. My gesture control strategy uses MediaPipe, with simple heuristics for navigation and detail viewing. I\'ve designed a heuristic mapping the actions with hand gestures. WebAssembly will be used by MediaPipe for enhanced performance. I will be installing the core dependencies for implementation, setting up the foundation for the project.\n\n\n**Installing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently installing the necessary libraries: `@react-three/drei`, `@mediapipe/tasks-vision`, and `framer-motion` for animations, and setting up the Express server for the backend. I need to handle image assets, too, but I\'m facing a constraint because the images provided are attached to the prompt, not directly accessible as files. I\'ll need to generate placeholder images locally, use placeholder URLs, or determine how to access the attached images, because the file system in AI studio cannot read from attachments.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Placeholders**\n\nI\'ve decided to use gradient placeholders, with CSS and Three.js text, for the initial demo. I\'ll include a note for the user to replace them with their images in the `/public` folder. If time allows I will use `generate_image`, or Unsplash if necessary.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m now setting up the Express server with Vite middleware, and adding the `/api/info` endpoint using Gemini with search grounding. I\'m also planning the `useHandTracking` hook for MediaPipe integration and preparing a Three.js scene for a rotating carousel with product cards using planes with textures (or CSS3D).\n\n\n**Constructing the Back-end**\n\nI\'m implementing the Tailwind-styled floating panels for product information and defensive coding practices to catch errors, like ensuring the webcam and WebGL context are valid. I\'m focusing on writing a complete `server.ts` file, and integrating Three.js with `@react-three/fiber` to scroll through product cards horizontally. I\'m taking the necessary steps to set up the appropriate packages.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 436770871
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
