oading errors, possibly CORS issues with the font URLs. To resolve this, I\'ll try using default Three.js text, or falling back to HTML-based text for guaranteed visibility. Alternatively, I will just remove the font prop altogether.\n\n\n**Simplifying Text Display**\n\nI\'m removing the custom font prop from the `Text` components. I\'ll increase the lighting\'s intensity to ensure text and products are visible. I\'ll now modify `Scene.tsx` to fix card visibility issues, lighten their background and increase brightness. I\'m also revising `useHandTracking.ts` to lower the swipe velocity threshold, making swipe detection more reliable and improving mirror logic.\n\n\n**Refining Swipe Calculation**\n\nI\'m now revising the swipe velocity logic in `useHandTracking.ts` to improve responsiveness. I\'m focusing on directly comparing current and previous X positions, considering a time threshold to avoid accidental swipes. The new approach uses a short sliding window to calculate delta X and detect swipes based on a velocity threshold within a specified time frame. I will test these new velocity thresholds soon. I also updated the onscreen instructions and implemented a DOM element cursor.\n\n\n**Optimizing Swipe Interaction**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new swipe gesture calculation in `useHandTracking.ts` to improve performance. I\'m storing hand position history and calculating delta X relative to the oldest position within a short time window. I\'ve lowered the threshold to 0.15 for swipe detection and will now be integrating a cursor update callback into the hook to improve the cursor\'s interaction in the app. I also plan to modify `Scene.tsx` and `App.tsx`, and will check the useFrame logic in Scene.tsx again.\n\n\n**Resolving Text Visibility**\n\nI\'m now diagnosing the product visibility issue, suspecting font loading failures as the core problem. The Drei `Text` component and its font URL are the likely culprits. I\'ll replace the font with a default sans-serif or